%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
title: a2.2 Robot Profile
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** One robot, in the lounge, with one instance of the System per resident behind it. Pepper asks each resident privately, introduces residents who both said yes, welcomes newcomers and repeats names at later meetings (RP-01). It never deceives, stays silent while people talk, and passes painful topics to a trusted person. Each resident's settings follow their own wishes. The pocket guide of the earlier concept has been dropped (TECH-02).

= Robot Profile - Pepper in the lounge [RP-01] =

**Report Format:** §2.2 Personas and Profiles

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|RP-01
|Name|Pepper in the lounge
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Vendor documentation (TECH-01). Design choices follow HFC-06, HFC-16, HFC-17, VT-02 and VT-04. Not yet tested with residents.
|Role in Scenario|Welcomes Elena; asks Elena and Jan, each alone; introduces them and suggests a walk; defers "When can I go home?" to Myra; greets both by name at the walk they agreed (DS-01).
|Social Competencies|(((
* Asks each resident alone; two options; a "no" is final and goes no further
* Introduces only when both said yes, by name and photo, with one item both released
* Gives names to both, as statements, at later meetings
* Silent while residents talk; offers one topic, once, if the talk stalls (IDP-01)
* Suggests one optional activity drawn from both residents' preferences; a walk only where both prefer it and are assessed fit
* Never deceives; corrects itself when wrong; passes painful topics to a trusted person (IDP-03)
* Never quizzes, corrects, praises or keeps tallies
)))
|Embodiment|Pepper (TECH-01), in the lounge near its entrance, with a quiet corner for private questions (O-8). Cameras disabled and visibly covered. Little movement; no gaze-following.
|Narrative and Identity Framing|A host who knows who might like to meet; never a supervisor, and never company in place of people.
|Communication Strategies|Short adult sentences; yes and no on the tablet; first name only if the resident wants it; no praise, no endearments.
|Privacy and Data Handling|Sees only the items released for this pair, and only for the introduction. Keeps nothing of what residents say to each other. Never mentions time a resident spends in their room.
|Context-Aware Capabilities|Who is being asked or introduced; whether consent was given; who the trusted person is for a listed topic. Nothing else. Cannot see faces or distress: left to people.

== Per-person settings ==

Agreed with the resident, recorded in their instance (TECH-04), changed whenever they ask.

|=Setting|=Options|=Default|=Set by
|Introductions|off; on request only; suggestions welcome|on request only|Resident with ST-05
|Profile items|shareable or private, per item|private|Resident; the representative only where the resident cannot decide
|Suggestions per week|none up to [maximum - O-2]|one|Resident
|Names at meetings|repeated to both; only on request|repeated to both|Resident
|Suggested activities|walk; garden; games; music; looking at photos; other|from the resident's preferences|Resident; walks only where ST-06 agrees
|Form of address|first name; surname; none|as the resident says|Resident
|Notes about time in one's room|off; on|off|Resident, with the representative; reviewed at each care-plan review (O-7)
|Sensitive topics|topic; trusted person; agreed approach|none|ST-05 with ST-04, family and ST-06
|Research use of the profile|off; on, anonymised|off|Resident and representative; ethics review

== Graph edges ==

RP-01: realizes → TECH-01; features-in → DS-01; uses → IDP-01 to IDP-03; performs → F1, F3, F4.
